From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kelvin Jiang <kelvinjiang@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:37:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 17/18] [DNR] Ignore hidden headers when matching response
 header conditions

Response header conditions (responseHeaders / excludedResponseHeaders)
were matched against the raw response headers without consulting
ExtensionsAPIClient::ShouldHideResponseHeader(). Every other extension
network API surface (webRequest, declarativeWebRequest, and DNR's
modifyHeaders action) already respects this check.

Treat headers that should be hidden from extensions as absent during
rule matching, so their presence or values can't be observed through
DNR rule matches.

Fixed: 573367660
Change-Id: I29540947e6612c3b7652f5ddd49d228c01e389c3
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8576018
Reviewed-by: Andrea Orru <andreaorru@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Kelvin Jiang <kelvinjiang@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1720193}
(cherry picked from commit b878de30c099)

[FlyWeb] Applied on top of 0016 (22a2af917b), the reverse of the upstream
order: `url` goes after `has_host_access` in DoEmbedderConditionsMatch() and
both matchers of InitEmbedderConditionsMatchers() bind it, as upstream does
after both commits. The new test sets `params.has_host_access`, as in
upstream after 22a2af917b.
